llama: the top set of the sampler chain

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9. The files of this patch are not touched by the other patches of this
repository.

Files:
    include/llama.h        llama_sampler_topset
    src/llama-sampler.cpp  the bound of the chain, the selection, the verify mode, the hook in llama_sampler_sample
    common/sampling.cpp    the hook in common_sampler::set_logits, the verify mode in common_sampler_sample

How to apply, from the llama.cpp root:

    git apply patches/hexagon-host/0003-llama-sampler-topset.patch
    cmake --build build-snapdragon -j

Only libllama.so and libllama-common.so change (the app links both).

Switch (environment variable):

    LLAMA_SAMPLER_TOPSET=N   0 = all the logits go to the chain (the previous behavior),
                             1 = the top set goes to the chain,
                             2 = the top set goes to the chain, and a clone of the chain runs on all the
                                 logits for a comparison of the two selected tokens

The problem

The sampler chain of the app is penalties, then top-k 20, top-p, temperature and dist (or greedy). The
vocabulary has 248320 tokens. For each token, llama_sampler_sample builds an array of 248320 candidates
(3 MB), the penalties sampler does one hash lookup for each candidate, and the top-k sampler does a
partial sort of the 248320 candidates. This work is the largest host cost of a token on the NPU.

The top set

A chain that cuts the candidates with top-k (or greedy) reads only the k best logits after the samplers
before the cut. The samplers before the cut move a bounded set of tokens by id: the penalties move the
tokens of the last-n window, and the logit bias moves its tokens. Let m = k + n_moved. A token outside the
m highest logits is not moved, and at least k tokens that are not moved have a logit equal to or higher
than its logit. Thus the top-k after the penalties is a subset of the m highest logits plus the moved
tokens, and the samplers after the cut (top-p, min-p, temperature, dist) see the same k candidates in the
same order. The selection is the same, and the random draw of dist is the same, thus the token stream is
the same. The one exception is a tie of the k-th and the (k+1)-th highest logits: the partial sort of
the full array and the partial sort of the top set can then keep a different token.

llama_sampler_topset finds m from the chain, and returns 0 when the chain needs all the logits: a grammar
or a reasoning budget (common_sampler applies them before the chain), dry, top-n-sigma, a dynamic
temperature (the entropy of all the candidates), a temperature of 0 or less before the cut, or no top-k
and no greedy sampler. The selection is one pass over the logits with a min-heap of m entries, thus
O(n_vocab) with a compare of each logit against the m-th best. The result is in token order, as the full
array is.

LLAMA_SAMPLER_TOPSET=2 clones the chain (with its random state), runs the clone on all the logits, and
compares the selected token with the one of the top set. A difference is a warn line. Every 64 tokens a
line gives the counts. The stream of the run is the one of the top set.
